      "hints": [
        "Treat the two inequalities together: do the same operation on all three parts.",
        "What happens to the inequality signs when you multiply or divide by a negative number?"
      ],
      "solution": {
        "modelAnswer": "Multiplying throughout by 4: \\(-2 \\le 3 - x < 4\\). Subtracting 3: \\(-5 \\le -x < 1\\). Multiplying by \\(-1\\) and reversing the signs: \\(5 \\ge x > -1\\), i.e. \\(-1 < x \\le 5\\), \\(x \\in R\\). On the number line: open circle at \\(-1\\), filled dot at 5, the segment between them darkened. Smallest integer \\(= 0\\), largest integer \\(= 5\\).",
        "finalAnswer": "Solution set \\(\\{x : -1 < x \\le 5,\\ x \\in R\\}\\); smallest integer 0, largest integer 5.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "n": 1,
            "title": "Clear the fraction",
            "expression": "-\\tfrac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\le 3 - x < 1 \\times 4 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; -2 \\le 3 - x < 4",
            "explanation": "Multiply every part by 4. Since 4 is positive, the signs do not change."
          },
          {
            "n": 2,
            "title": "Isolate the x-term",
            "expression": "-2 - 3 \\le -x < 4 - 3 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; -5 \\le -x < 1",
            "explanation": "Subtract 3 from every part."
          },
          {
            "n": 3,
            "title": "Divide by −1",
            "expression": "5 \\ge x > -1",
            "result": "-1 < x \\le 5",
            "explanation": "Multiplying by \\(-1\\) reverses both inequality signs. Read from left to right, \\(x\\) is greater than \\(-1\\) and at most 5.",
            "rule": "Multiplying or dividing an inequation by a negative number reverses the sign."
          },
          {
            "n": 4,
            "title": "Number line",
            "explanation": "Draw an open circle at \\(-1\\) (not included, because \\(x > -1\\)) and a filled dot at 5 (included, because \\(x \\le 5\\)), and darken the line between them.",
            "diagramId": "nl1"
          },
          {
            "n": 5,
            "title": "Integers in the set",
            "expression": "x \\in \\{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}",
            "result": "\\text{smallest} = 0, \\ \\text{largest} = 5",
            "explanation": "\\(-1\\) is excluded, so the smallest integer is 0; 5 is included, so the largest integer is 5.",
            "isFinal": true
          }
        ],
        "commonMistakes": [
          "Not reversing the signs when multiplying by \\(-1\\), giving \\(-5 \\le x < 1\\).",
          "Swapping open and filled circles on the number line (filling \\(-1\\) or leaving 5 open).",
          "Giving \\(-1\\) as the smallest integer even though \\(x > -1\\)."
        ],
        "alternativeMethods": [
          {
            "title": "Solve the two parts separately",
            "description": "\\(-\\tfrac{1}{2} \\le \\tfrac{3-x}{4} \\Rightarrow -2 \\le 3 - x \\Rightarrow x \\le 5\\), and \\(\\tfrac{3-x}{4} < 1 \\Rightarrow 3 - x < 4 \\Rightarrow x > -1\\). Combining: \\(-1 < x \\le 5\\)."
          }
        ]
      },
